# sudo -D in DIR, refuses an unknown cp/mv/install/ln option, treats $HOME and ~ as unreadable once the command
# reassigns HOME, and refuses a variable whose literal head parents or sits under a tracked project; and it
# states the contract plainly (best-effort against known write forms, allow by default) with the current list of
# unmodelled writers that pass, the same paragraph the hook header, hooks/README.md and docs/install.md carry.
# Other hosts have no Bash-side guard, so this stays romp's. Prose only; pinned by the host's
